# The build context for Dockerfile.dev, as an allow-list: the image copies only the lock, the
# project file and its two scripts, and the source arrives at start as a clone in /workspace.
# So nothing else (a venv, `.invective/` killers, bench results, a stray secret) can reach a
# local build. infra builds from this repo's git URL, whose context is the tracked tree.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!docker-child-init.dev.sh
!docker-login.dev.sh
